  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Dell Federal Systems L P has $1.2B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, from 453 awards with an average award size of $2.7M, and obligations are down 6.7% year over year. Dell Federal Systems L P received $1.6B in FY21, $1.7B in FY22, $1.4B in FY23, $1.5B in FY24, and $1.3B in FY25, showing multi-year scale before the current FY2026 total. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer in FY2026 to date with $548M, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $251M, the Department of Health and Human Services with $138M, and the Department of Defense with $135M. Software Publishers is the largest market for Dell Federal Systems L P in FY2026 to date with $995M in obligations, followed by a second Software Publishers entry at $125M and Other Computer Related Services at $61.9M. Electronic Computer Manufacturing and Computer Storage Device Manufacturing appear among the top markets with $54.5M and $4.6M respectively. This profile reflects concentrated demand in software and IT equipment across a small set of federal buyers.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies drive Dell Federal Systems L P revenue?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs drives the most revenue for Dell Federal Systems L P with $548M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security and the Department of Health and Human Services follow with $251M and $138M respectively, while the Department of Defense accounts for $135M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and products account for Dell Federal Systems L P obligations?",
        "body": "Software Publishers is the dominant market for Dell Federal Systems L P with $995M in FY2026 to date, supplemented by another Software Publishers entry at $125M and Other Computer Related Services at $61.9M. Electronic Computer Manufacturing and Computer Storage Device Manufacturing also appear among the top markets with $54.5M and $4.6M."
      }
    ]
  },
